# More precise explanations for small, single-purpose guides.
context={
'backup-status':'Preparing means Oath is constructing the encrypted backup. Uploading means the cloud operation is still in progress. An error or unavailable state must not be counted as a completed backup.|Review the status for each wallet you intend to preserve. Keep its backup password and any recovery passphrase independently; a successful upload alone does not mean you remember how to decrypt it.',
'icloud-troubleshooting':'A simulator without an Apple Account shows the unavailable state illustrated here. The screenshot is not evidence that a file was uploaded or restored.|If the backup is listed but will not decrypt, check the password for that specific file. Changing the app passcode does not change an old backup file’s encryption password.',
'move-to-new-phone':'Import or restore each distinct wallet, not only the wallet that happened to be active. Preserve names, any added BIP-39 passphrases and supported address/path choices needed to recognize the same accounts.|Wait for data refresh, then compare full public addresses on the same network. A matching nickname or a nonzero balance is not sufficient evidence that every old account was restored.',
'enable-passcode':'The passcode is six digits and protects local access to Oath. It does not replace an offline recovery phrase, imported private key or encrypted backup.|If the confirmation does not match, re-enter the intended code carefully. Once setup finishes, verify that Passcode is enabled before leaving security settings.',
'change-passcode':'Verifying the current passcode establishes authority to change local protection. The new code does not alter blockchain addresses or change the password of a previously uploaded backup file.|If you cancel or the change fails, do not assume the new code was saved. Follow the visible result and keep the current recovery material safe.',
'disable-security':'Turning off biometrics alone leaves app-passcode protection available. Turning off the passcode changes the local protection policy and requires the corresponding confirmation.|Use App Switcher Privacy and Hide Balances independently where appropriate. Neither is a replacement for authentication or an independent recovery backup.',
'auto-lock':'The delay controls when Oath requires authentication after leaving the foreground. Choose Immediately for the shortest grace period.|Restarting the app requires authentication when passcode protection is enabled. The delay is not a promise that signing or sensitive settings will skip their own confirmation.',
'lock-now':'The lock action ends the current unlocked session instead of waiting for the configured background delay. The next user must complete the applicable unlock flow.|Locking is local protection. It does not disconnect all dApps, revoke token access or cancel a transaction already broadcast to a network.',
'hide-balances':'Hidden amounts are a display preference, not deletion or encryption of public blockchain information. Other people may still look up the public addresses.|Check any exported image before sharing it. An explorer link can reveal amounts even when the app’s displayed values are hidden.',
'reset-app':'Reset removes local wallets and associated app data and returns the installation to Welcome. It cannot reverse transfers, erase public chain history or revoke on-chain allowances.|An encrypted iCloud backup is a separate file. Keep its original password and any other required recovery information if you want to restore afterward.|If you only want to remove one wallet while keeping others, use Wallets instead. The last-wallet removal has its own Recently Deleted confirmation sequence.',
'asset-order':'Price availability can change the ordering: an asset without a usable quote may not sit beside similarly valuable priced assets. Sorting is not a safety or authenticity rating.|Use the active filters and Search to find assets intentionally; an asset moving down the list does not mean it was sold or removed.',
'asset-information':'A token’s network and complete contract, mint, type or issuer reference are its identity. A symbol such as USDC can identify different deployments on different networks.|Project descriptions, logos and external websites are metadata, not guarantees. Read the hostname before following a link and never provide recovery material to a project page.',
'bitcoin-address-types':'Taproot, Native SegWit, wrapped SegWit and Legacy use different address formats and derivations within a compatible Bitcoin wallet. Selecting a type does not convert coins into another network.|An imported single key or account-scoped extended key can support fewer choices. Use the choices actually offered for that wallet; do not assume a full recovery-phrase account was restored.|When comparing an older receipt, retain its original address and transaction ID. New receive addresses can differ while still belonging to the same supported wallet.',
'bitcoin-gap-limit':'Address discovery scans a bounded sequence of unused HD addresses. Large runs of intentionally unused addresses can place later activity outside ordinary discovery.|Keep records of any unusual account index or derivation choices used in the original wallet. A single imported key cannot reproduce a full HD address tree.|Do not repeatedly generate and discard addresses as a test of recovery. Compare known public addresses and use the supported receive selection.',
'solana-address-path':'Phantom and Trust Wallet conventions derive different accounts from the same recovery phrase. Selecting the path changes which Solana address the receive screen shows and which account its data follows.|Before changing a path, finish any pending send or dApp review. Return to the dApp and reconnect or choose the matching account if it expects a different address.|A single imported Solana key can only expose its original account; it does not gain both derivations by selecting a menu option.',
'copy-transaction-id':'Copying returns the complete transaction identifier even when the visible row is abbreviated. Paste it into the explorer for that same network, not a different chain with a similar format.|A transaction ID is public, but sharing it can reveal associated account activity. It is useful for support and payment verification; recovery words are not needed.',
'view-explorer':'Check the explorer hostname and network before reading the result. Some transactions contain several transfers, approvals or contract events, so the first displayed amount may not describe the whole operation.|An explorer is external content. Close it to return to Oath and avoid any advertising or links requesting recovery material.',
'edit-contact':'Changing a contact only edits the saved label or destination. It does not change an earlier transaction or notify the other person.|Before replacing a stored address, confirm the new address with the recipient through a trusted channel. Keep network-specific labels clear so you do not reuse the wrong deposit destination.',
'delete-contact':'Deleting a contact removes the local address-book entry. It does not delete the wallet controlling that address, reverse payments or remove public activity.|If you need the contact later, add its verified public address again. Check that no unfinished transfer is relying on an outdated saved recipient.',
'search-contacts':'Search by a recognizable contact name or saved public destination. If a contact is absent, clear the query and inspect the full address book before creating a duplicate.|In Send, recipient suggestions are scoped to the selected network. A contact’s address on another chain may not be a valid choice for the current transfer.',
'request-feature':'Describe the problem you want to solve, where in Oath it happens and what outcome would help. Include the current app version when relevant.|A feature request is a proposal, not a promise of availability. Continue to use the supported flow described by the current guide until a release adds the feature.',
'report-bug':'Include the app version, device/iOS version, screen, exact steps and nonsecret error text. For a transaction issue, add its network and public transaction ID if one exists.|A screenshot can help, but review it first for balances, names and other private information. Never attach recovery phrases, keys, passwords, pairing URIs or raw signed payloads.|If a submission is pending or uncertain, check its existing transaction before attempting another transfer while waiting for support.',
'contact-support':'Explain what you were trying to do and what happened instead. Public network and transaction identifiers can help diagnose a payment issue without exposing wallet secrets.|Opening an email draft does not send it. Review the recipients, body and attachments in your mail app before choosing Send.|Oath support cannot recover a forgotten recovery phrase or safely ask you to reveal a private key. Treat unsolicited requests for those secrets as untrusted.',
'about-legal':'Use the displayed version when reporting a bug or comparing a guide with your installed app. Older archived release articles can describe controls that have since changed.|Open the current Terms and Privacy Policy from the app when you need the applicable documents. A help article is usage guidance and does not replace those documents.',
'arc-usdc':'Native USDC on Arc is the network’s base asset in this integration. An ERC-20 USDC deployment on Ethereum, Base or another network is not interchangeable with that Arc balance.|When sending, review the fee units and exact network rather than assuming ETH always pays gas on an EVM-compatible chain.|Discovery of other Arc tokens and their quotes depends on supported provider coverage. An incomplete index must not be interpreted as proof that no tokens exist.',
'robinhood-chain':'Check the chain identity in the asset information and receiving flow. This account is an on-chain wallet account, not a brokerage login or a link to a centralized account.|Use the network’s native fee asset for supported transfers and review the fee before confirming.|If a token or history entry is missing, compare the public explorer result and retry discovery. Native balance success alone does not prove complete token or history coverage.',
'permanently-delete-wallet':'The displayed deletion deadline is a remaining local recovery window, not a blockchain expiry. Permanent deletion closes that local recovery route immediately.|Read the selected count and names again at confirmation. If you are uncertain about a backup, cancel and restore the wallet first so you can verify its recovery options.',
}
for slug,text in context.items():body(slug,text)
